 "stimulus_html": "Simplify the following:",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505748,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"{\\left( {\\frac{{{7^9}}}{{{{10}^5} \\times {6^3}}}} \\right)^8}\">{\\left( {\\frac{{{7^9}}}{{{{10}^5} \\times {6^3}}}} \\right)^8}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"{\\left( {\\frac{{{7^9}}}{{{{10}^5} \\times {6^3}}}} \\right)^8}\"></span></p>\n<p>Use the exponent distributive rule. When you have a fraction, <span data-math=\"\\frac{a}{b}\"></span>, raised to an exponent, <i>n</i>, then <span data-math=\"{\\left( {\\frac{a}{b}} \\right)^n} = \\frac{{{a^n}}}{{{b^n}}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{{\\left( {{7^9}} \\right)}^8}}}{{{{\\left( {{{10}^5} \\times {6^3}} \\right)}^8}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Use the distributive rule for exponents in the denominator: <span data-math=\"{\\left( {a \\times b} \\right)^n} = {a^n} \\times {b^n}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{{\\left( {{7^9}} \\right)}^8}}}{{{{\\left( {{{10}^5}} \\right)}^8} \\times {{\\left( {{6^3}} \\right)}^8}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Use the power rule. If you raise a non-zero base to an exponent <i>n</i>, and raise that to another exponent, <i>m</i>, you get the base raised to the product of the exponents.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\left( {{a^n}} \\right)^m} = {a^{\\left( {n \\times m} \\right)}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{7^{72}}}}{{{{10}^{40}} \\times {6^{24}}}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{{{7^{72}}}}{{{{10}^{40}} \\times {6^{24}}}}\">\\frac{{{7^{72}}}}{{{{10}^{40}} \\times {6^{24}}}}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
